<h2 id="bottom-line">Bottom Line</h2>

<p>E Ink's forecast cut is a rare, clear window into the machinery behind your reading device. Surging memory prices are delaying e-reader launches and putting upward pressure on prices, and even the transition to color e-ink is moving more slowly than the industry hoped. None of that makes EPUB reading any less excellent — your library of EPUB files is completely portable and unaffected by hardware economics.</p>

<p>The smartest response is to buy with intention, not urgency: set a budget, decide monochrome versus color up front, compare ecosystems, and remember that the best upgrade is often a well-organized EPUB library on the device you already own.</p>
